# PCMCI-Based Feature-Selection Study Across 250 Grid Cells in Morocco

Code and results accompanying the paper "A PCMCI-Based Feature-Selection Study Across 250 Grid Cells in Morocco" (submitted to Solar Energy).

## Contents

- `code/` — the full analysis pipeline, 11 scripts covering data preparation and causal discovery (PCMCI), model fitting, selector comparison, threshold sweeps, seasonal/cloud-regime strata analysis, a no-cloud ablation, rolling-origin cross-validation, assumption checks (stationarity, collinearity), a nonlinear conditional-independence check (CMIknn), and spatiotemporal block bootstrap uncertainty estimates.
- `results/` — derived CSV outputs from each pipeline stage (selection comparisons, threshold sweep tables, strata skill/MBE, ablation tables, rolling-origin fold results, stationarity/collinearity diagnostics, CMIknn test results, spatiotemporal bootstrap output, and daily predictions).

## Requirements

Python 3.x with `numpy`, `pandas`, `scikit-learn`, and `tigramite`.

## Citation

If you use this code or data, please cite the paper (full citation to be added upon publication).

